<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĕon</span></b> , ontis, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λέων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of a town near Syracuse</i>, now <i>Magnisi; acc.</i> Leonta, <i><span class="en">Liv. 24,
				39, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A ruler of Phlius</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				5, 3, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A celebrated painter</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				11, 40, § 141</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
